me is `--model`, read from `/proc/<pid>/maps` (dev, inode, pathname), re-opened by that pathname with `O_NOFOLLOW`, accepted only when `fstat()` shows the same dev and inode and a regular file of the mapped size, then hashed; written into the receipt at `:2003` while the child is running (`:1763` default `None`, never a check id — the v1–v5 check lists are unchanged). The frozen counter `tools/round50-replay-bind-audit.py` (sha256 `ff6ac2ace541ea35a4d240ceebb019653c11a2a08c025e514770f3f94a9c5e89`) starts each replay through a `python3 -I -c` invoker with an environment of `PATH`/`LANG`/`HOME`/`XDG_CACHE_HOME`/`TMPDIR` (last three under `--scratch`), the proxy variables when it has them, and two canaries (`KAMA_R50_CANARY`, a `PYTHONPATH` `sitecustomize.py` that stamps `<pid> <argv>`), and while the replay holds its server it checks the exe digest, a LISTEN socket whose inode is one of the pid's fds, a fresh nonce against its own decoding of the model's tokenizer vocabulary, descent from the replay process, canary absence in the process and its parent plus an empty marker file, and the mapped dev/inode/pathname hashed to the frozen model; after release it joins the observed pid with the rerun receipt's `child_pid`, reads the same dev and inode back from `model_mapping`, and requires the pid gone and the port refusing. Build-time value (`.ufo/waves/round-50/measured/c1-build.out`): `bind=1 teardown=1 newrow=1 bound=3/3 met=True` — three replays held servers on pids 2876695/2920026/2958773 (ports 40197/41321/35623), each exe+listen+tree+env+mapped ok with a nonce round-trip, mapping dev 103:05 with inodes 1082269665/613853333/1149932363, teardown `invoker SIGKILLed with 3 descendants; after 0.10 s alive [] port refuses ok`, newrow `3 rows new since base; 1 name proc_pid_maps(5): ['| S496 |']`. Base control (`.ufo/waves/round-50/controls/base.c1.out` at `26ecba64`): `bind=0 teardown=0 newrow=0 bound=0/3 met=False` — each receipt's server parent carries `KAMA_R50_CANARY`, `model_mapping None`, the planted `sitecustomize` imported by one interpreter, and after SIGKILL of the invoker `after 30.06 s alive [531059, 568483, 573554] port ACCEPTS`. Limits (preregistration): the mapped check compares the maps dev/inode with a `stat()` of the pathname and hashes that path now, so a file rewritten in place with identical bytes is indistinguishable and a filesystem whose maps dev differs from `st_dev` (btrfs subvolumes) fails closed; the env leg plants two canaries, not `LD_PRELOAD` or a modified `python` on `PATH`; the teardown leg kills the invoker once, during the hold, not during download or readiness.
