/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kaidoku-shokunin/SKILL.md:788:- **34. A receipt that exits 0 is bound to the world it claims: its label, its own counts, the measured tree and the pinned bytes, and it is written through a name no planted symlink can occupy.** <!-- receipt-world-binding v1 --> The receipt-world-binding failure class is the one where a receipt, its stdout and its rc agree with each other while none of the three is bound to the world they describe, so the agreement is self-consistent and false. Round 94 measured three instances of it and each is carried into this block. M94-e is the frozen agreement counter `tools/round-94/c1-receipt-agreement.py` admitting a receipt pair whose label is rewritten consistently in both files and a wholly fabricated triple: it checks receipt↔stdout↔rc agreement and the predicted met/exit per run name, and it never binds the label to the frozen expect string nor recomputes it from the counts, so the pinned counter scores all four committed forgeries as a pass (`.ufo/waves/round-95/pre/c1-old-counter-admits-at-base.json`: valid 4, agree 4, predicted 4, met true). M94-f is the base receipts' short `--rev`, which nothing validated against the tree it claimed (`.ufo/waves/round-94/pre/c1-base-v3-pos.json`). SentinelWrite F1 is the round-94 writer's `open(<json-out>.tmp, "w")` following a symlink planted at the predictable temporary name, so the receipt it wrote was valid while the victim file was overwritten (`.ufo/waves/round-95/pre/c1-symlink-v4-at-base.json`: `victim_intact false`, verdict `followed-symlink`). The round-95 instruments answer the three separately: `tools/round-95/c1-agreement-v2.py` keeps every round-94 atom and adds four typed world bindings, `tools/round-95/stop-boundary-repair-battery-v5.py` writes its receipt through a `mkstemp` name in the receipt's own directory and re-reads and re-verifies that receipt before it may exit 0, and `tools/round-95/symlink-probe.py` measures the public write path against a planted symlink (`.ufo/waves/round-95/l1/scores/c1-symlink-v5-at-4bda1d1dd3788973f10e61212b70df18b3b14ea0.json`: `victim_intact true`). The table routes each failure class to the signature it produces, the guard that answers it, and the criterion that names the rule.
